        "mission_intent": "Team, we need a comprehensive collection requirement stood up against Mexico-based transnational criminal organizations\u2014specifically the Sinaloa Cartel and New Generation Jalisco Cartel\u2014focused on their fentanyl and synthetic opioid production and trafficking pipelines into the United States. The requirement should prioritize intelligence on smuggling methodologies at official ports of entry along the southwest border, including concealment techniques in passenger vehicles and commercial tractor-trailers, as well as any anticipated shifts in smuggling routes or tradecraft these organizations may adopt in response to heightened U.S. border security posture. We also need collection threads on upstream precursor chemical sourcing networks, particularly any ties to PRC-based suppliers active since at least 2020. Given that CDC provisional data showed a roughly one-third decline in synthetic opioid overdose fatalities through October 2024\u2014possibly linked to naloxone availability\u2014please incorporate indicators that help us assess whether this trend reflects actual supply disruption or merely improved harm reduction on the demand side. Nominate all relevant HUMINT, SIGINT, and OSINT platforms; coordinate with DEA and CBP liaisons for deconfliction. I need the full collection plan with priority intelligence requirements, nominated sources, and reporting timelines submitted to the division chief by close of business Friday for review before it goes to the National HUMINT Requirements Tasking Center.",
